node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
# Demo Driver scratch — every starter's demo.beats.json types its spec into
# live/ so the committed crewhaus.yaml is never touched on camera.
live/
**/live/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.local
# .crewhaus/ — only runtime artifacts are ignored. User-authored
# slash commands, skills, sub-agents, and settings under .crewhaus/ ARE
# source code and committed (drives the showcase demos). The **/ forms
# matter: running a demo from inside its own directory writes runtime
# artifacts into that demo's nested .crewhaus/.
**/.crewhaus/sessions/
**/.crewhaus/tool-results/
**/.crewhaus/events.jsonl
**/.crewhaus/*.jsonl
**/.crewhaus/cache/
**/.crewhaus/evals/
**/.crewhaus/memories/
**/.crewhaus/feedback/
**/.crewhaus/specs/
**/.crewhaus/audit/
**/.crewhaus/graphs/
**/.crewhaus/research/
# Written by a live demo-driver take (continuity state, durable steps,
# flywheel runs). state/ is the continuity store: continuity is ON BY DEFAULT
# in 0.4.0, so EVERY run of EVERY starter writes .crewhaus/state/<agent>/
# handoff.md — measured by running `crewhaus run crewhaus.yaml` inside
# starters/cli with no memory: block in the spec at all.
# trash/ is where the continuity store's clear() (/clear-plan, /clear-focus)
# moves files; it is never source. Note .crewhaus/datasets/ is deliberately
# NOT ignored — starters/eval vendors its dataset there — so a take that
# distills a new one shows up for review.
**/.crewhaus/idempotency/
**/.crewhaus/flywheel/
**/.crewhaus/state/
**/.crewhaus/trash/
# starters/trader — the paper broker's runtime state (ledger + journal)
**/.paper-broker/
.claude/
# Editor-local config. A Demo Driver launch config has to name the local path of
# a demo-driver checkout (github.com/crewhaus/demo-driver), which is specific to
# one machine's layout and broken for anyone who clones this repo on its own — so
# it stays out of git. Install the extension from a .vsix instead (DEMO-DRIVERS.md).
.vscode/
